1. a11y (for checker-a11y): with the Current card applyable there can now be
   TWO visible buttons with the identical accessible name "Apply this option"
   (Current plan card + a headline card) differing only by their containing
   article's h5. Master could already render two such buttons across the two
   headline cards, so this is not new, but the Current-plan case is newly
   reachable. Markup/classes for the new control are byte-identical to the
   existing one (same `whatif-spending-option` template block), so focus ring
   and target size are inherited unchanged.
2. Test-strength note: criterion 3's compare is `json.Marshal` of
   models.WhatIfSettings, which omits three `json:"-"` fields
   (CurrentAge, SpouseAge at internal/models/whatif.go:113-114, and
   BracketFillFeedback at :1737). Drift confined to those derived/non-
   persisted fields would not be caught. The apply handler does not assign
   them, and all three fields the criterion names are mutation-proven, so
   this is a residual-risk note only.
3. `make check` takes ~2 min (storage package alone is 71s); worth knowing
   before the final pass.
